2462"} "Marc Zwiebler"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "China’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/121932"} "Chen Long"] ", the number two ranked player, dropped only one set, when the eighth seeded Korean " [:a {:href "/athletes/123526"} "Son Wan-Ho"] " won the second set of their quarter-final. All his other matches, apart from one walkover, were achieved with straight sets wins. In the final he beat his long-time rival " [:a {:href "/athletes/105855"} "Lee Chong Wei"] " of Malaysia, the then number one ranked player, 21-18, 21-18. The bronze medal went to " [:a {:href "/athletes/133435"} "Viktor Axelsen"] " from Denmark, who overcame the defending Olympic champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/105835"} "Lin Dan"] " of China, who was ranked one place above the Dane."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/121932"} "Chen Long"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/105855"} "Lee Chong Wei"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/MAS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/MAS.png"}] "MAS"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/133435"} "Viktor Axelsen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/DEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/DEN.png"}] "DEN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/105835"} "Lin Dan